#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""apod gh broker: runs gh, and git fetches and pushes to GitHub, on the host for apod pods.

Pods hold no GitHub token. Each pod gets a session (a persona, a host gh account and a scope of
repositories, owners and projects) and a unix socket. The pod's gh is a shim that sends its
arguments to that socket, and git's github.com remotes go through it too. The broker turns each
request into actions ("pr create", "api GET /repos/{repo}/pulls", "graphql mutation addComment",
"git push branch") and targets (repositories, owners, projects). It runs the real gh with the
account's token, or forwards the git request with it, when the persona allows every action and
every target is in scope. Anything else waits for approval (apod gh ui, apod gh allow) until it
times out.

  apod-broker serve                 run the broker in the foreground
  apod-broker register ...          start a session (used by apod; starts the broker if needed)
  apod-broker unregister ID         end a session
  apod-broker sessions|pending|log [-f] [-n N]|allow ID [--session|--persona]|deny ID
  apod-broker ui|grants [rm PERSONA ACTION]|personas|stop
"""
